137
00:10:39,160 --> 00:10:44,360
The problem was that the churches of New York City

138
00:10:44,460 --> 00:10:48,560
or the churches of Boston or the churches of Philadelphia

139
00:10:48,561 --> 00:10:53,900
in the center of town, and they could no longer fit more people

140
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:57,600
into their graveyards.

141
00:10:57,700 --> 00:11:02,700
In 1831, Mount Auburn in Cambridge, Massachusetts,

142
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:05,520
was at the leading edge of the new cemetery movement

143
00:11:05,620 --> 00:11:06,320
in America.

144
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:13,420
The goal soon echoed in Brooklyn's Greenwood Cemetery

145
00:11:13,520 --> 00:11:18,560
in 1838 was to move the cemetery out of the city.

146
00:11:18,561 --> 00:11:22,660
and also make cemeteries attractive places that mourners

147
00:11:22,661 --> 00:11:27,160
would want to visit. The time period when cemeteries

148
00:11:27,161 --> 00:11:30,300
really became tourist attractions dates from the 1830s

149
00:11:30,301 --> 00:11:33,800
when they created the first of these very large and beautifully

150
00:11:33,801 --> 00:11:36,820
landscaped cemeteries on the outskirts of major cities.

151
00:11:36,821 --> 00:11:40,820
They actually served the function of city parks before city parks

152
00:11:40,821 --> 00:11:45,120
